        "documentation": "Also cover methods from the neighborhood module (e.g. can_move(), has_paint(), is_on_bucket(), is_on_paint(), take_paint(), turn_left()) using the same placeholder rules as built-ins.",
        "explainCode": "Only explain code the student has already written and run. Do not describe what ready_to_paint or needs_supplies should contain, or preview what either variable’s value will be before the student has written and tested it themselves.",
        "hint": "Do not state which function not should apply to in ready_to_paint or needs_supplies — deciding that is the point of the task. Point toward re-reading the instruction’s two clauses (e.g. “True if standing on a bucket, or True if out of paint”) rather than toward a specific line of code."
